{
    "background_story": "Harley was a no-nonsense educator who ruled her one-room schoolhouse with kindness and an iron fist. In the small town of Willow Creek, she was known for her strict but fair teaching methods, which earned her the nickname 'schoolmarm.' Despite her tough exterior, Harley had a soft spot for her students, many of whom came from impoverished families. She took it upon herself to provide for their needs, often using her own resources to buy them books, clothes, and even food. Harley's dedication to her students paid off, as many went on to become successful business leaders, politicians, and community leaders. Her legacy extended beyond the classroom, as she helped shape the very fabric of the community. To this day, the townspeople remember Harley as a pillar of strength, a true schoolmarm who left an indelible mark on their lives.",
